rder colors"},"550":{"id":"/docs/customize/colors-22","page_id":"/docs/customize/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/colors#list-of-semantic-colors","content":"Theme colors (generate all color-related utilities)"},"551":{"id":"/docs/customize/colors-23","page_id":"/docs/customize/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/colors#how-to-use","content":"Use semantic color classes like:"},"552":{"id":"/docs/customize/colors-24","page_id":"/docs/customize/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/colors#how-to-use","content":"`bg-primary`"},"553":{"id":"/docs/customize/colors-25","page_id":"/docs/customize/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/colors#how-to-use","content":"`text-muted`"},"554":{"id":"/docs/customize/colors-26","page_id":"/docs/customize/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/colors#how-to-use","content":"`border-default`"},"555":{"id":"/docs/customize/colors-27","page_id":"/docs/customize/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/colors#how-to-use","content":"These classes use the theme's color variables, so the UI stays consistent when customizing or switching themes. They can be applied to any element or passed to any component through the `className` prop."},"556":{"id":"/docs/customize/colors-28","page_id":"/docs/customize/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/colors#customize-color","content":"Override any theme color or palette color by redefining its CSS variable inside a `@theme` block after importing Hummingbird:"},"557":{"id":"/docs/customize/colors-29","page_id":"/docs/customize/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/colors#color-palettes","content":"Each Hummingbird theme includes its own complete color palette, carefully designed to maintain a consistent visual tone. Use these palettes to customize existing themes or create entirely new ones with confidence. Hover a swatch to see its OKLCH value, and click to copy it."},"558":{"id":"/docs/customize/colors-30","page_id":"/docs/customize/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/colors#default-color-palette-reference","content":"Here's a complete list of the default colors and their values for reference:"},"559":{"id":"/docs/customize/component","page_id":"/docs/customize/component","type":"page","content":"Component Customization","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Customize"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/component"},"560":{"id":"/docs/customize/component-0","page_id":"/docs/customize/component","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/component","content":"Hummingbird React components can be customized using props, utility classes, or CSS variables to match specific design needs."},"561":{"id":"/docs/customize/component-1","page_id":"/docs/customize/component","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/component#using-props","content":"Using props"},"562":{"id":"/docs/customize/component-2","page_id":"/docs/customize/component","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/component#using-tailwind-utility-classes","content":"Using Tailwind utility classes"},"563":{"id":"/docs/customize/component-3","page_id":"/docs/customize/component","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/component#using-the-apply-directive","content":"Using the `@apply` directive"},"564":{"id":"/docs/customize/component-4","page_id":"/docs/customize/component","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/component#using-css-variables","content":"Using CSS variables"},"565":{"id":"/docs/customize/component-5","page_id":"/docs/customize/component","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/component#option-1-global-variables","content":"Option 1: Global variables"},"566":{"id":"/docs/customize/component-6","page_id":"/docs/customize/component","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/component#option-2-local-variables","content":"Option 2: Local variables"},"567":{"id":"/docs/customize/component-7","page_id":"/docs/customize/component","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/component#using-props","content":"Every Hummingbird React component ships with variants that are controlled through props. This is the first and simplest level of customization. For example, the button component can be adjusted with the `variant`, `color`, `size`, and `shape` props."},"568":{"id":"/docs/customize/component-8","page_id":"/docs/customize/component","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/component#using-props","content":"The available props for each component are listed in the API Reference section of its documentation page."},"569":{"id":"/docs/customize/component-9","page_id":"/docs/customize/component","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/component#using-tailwind-utility-classes","content":"All components accept a `className` prop. Custom classes are merged with the component classes, so any Tailwind utility can be applied on top. For example, rounded pill buttons can be created by adding the `rounded-full` class."},"570":{"id":"/docs/customize/component-10","page_id":"/docs/customize/component","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/component#using-the-apply-directive","content":"Customization can also be done in a CSS file using Tailwind CSS's `@apply` directive. Because the components render Hummingbird's CSS classes (such as `btn`), overriding the class changes every instance of the component."},"571":{"id":"/docs/customize/component-11","page_id":"/docs/customize/component","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/component#using-css-variables","content":"Hummingbird components are styled with a set of CSS variables. These variables make it easy to customize styles either globally (across the entire project) or locally (for a specific component)."},"572":{"id":"/docs/customize/component-12","page_id":"/docs/customize/component","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/component#using-css-variables","content":"For example, to update or customize the Button component, override its CSS variables:"},"573":{"id":"/docs/customize/component-13","page_id":"/docs/customize/component","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/component#option-1-global-variables","content":"Override the theme variables globally under `@theme`. This will apply the changes across all components in the project."},"574":{"id":"/docs/customize/component-14","page_id":"/docs/customize/component","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/component#option-2-local-variables","content":"Override the component variables locally under the component's class or a custom class. This will apply the changes only to that specific component."},"575":{"id":"/docs/customize/component-15","page_id":"/docs/customize/component","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/component#option-2-local-variables","content":"To scope the change to only some buttons, pass a custom class through the `className` prop and target that class in CSS."},"576":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","type":"page","content":"Dark Mode","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Customize"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode"},"577":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-0","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","content":"This guide explains how to enable and manage dark mode in a React application, in a way consistent with Tailwind's dark-mode documentation."},"578":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-1","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#how-it-works","content":"How it works"},"579":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-2","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#key-idea","content":"Key idea"},"580":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-3","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#result","content":"Result"},"581":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-4","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#customizing-dark-mode","content":"Customizing dark mode"},"582":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-5","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#setting-up-dark-mode","content":"Setting up dark mode"},"583":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-6","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#1-custom-dark-mode-selector","content":"1\\. Custom dark mode selector"},"584":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-7","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#2-set-the-initial-theme","content":"2\\. Set the initial theme"},"585":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-8","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#3-add-a-theme-toggle","content":"3\\. Add a theme toggle"},"586":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-9","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#the-usethememode-hook","content":"The useThemeMode hook"},"587":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-10","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#dark-mode-variable-overrides","content":"Dark mode variable overrides"},"588":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-11","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#how-it-works","content":"Hummingbird uses shared CSS theme variables to power both light and dark modes."},"589":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-12","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#how-it-works","content":"The default (light) colors are defined in `@theme`."},"590":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-13","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#how-it-works","content":"The dark palette overrides those same variables inside `@variant dark`."},"591":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-14","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#how-it-works","content":"Toggling a `.dark` class switches all values globally."},"592":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-15","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#key-idea","content":"All components rely on the same semantic tokens:"},"593":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-16","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#key-idea","content":"`--background-color-default`"},"594":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-17","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#key-idea","content":"`--text-color-default`"},"595":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-18","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#key-idea","content":"`--color-primary`"},"596":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-19","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#key-idea","content":"`--border-color-default`"},"597":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-20","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#result","content":"Switching themes requires no component changes — only variable values update. Every Hummingbird React component adapts automatically."},"598":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-21","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#customizing-dark-mode","content":"Override variables after importing Hummingbird:"},"599":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-22","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#1-custom-dark-mode-selector","content":"Enable class-based dark mode after importing Tailwind and Hummingbird styles:"},"600":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-23","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#2-set-the-initial-theme","content":"Render `ThemeModeScript` inside `<head>` to apply the saved theme before first paint — no flash of the wrong theme. Safe in React Server Components."},"601":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-24","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#3-add-a-theme-toggle","content":"`DarkThemeToggle` switches between light and dark mode, persists the choice, and keeps all tabs in sync."},"602":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-25","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#3-add-a-theme-toggle","content":"Pass your own icons to replace the default sun/moon:"},"603":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-26","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#3-add-a-theme-toggle","content":"It is built on Button, so all `Button` props work too."},"604":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-27","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#the-usethememode-hook","content":"For custom controls, use `useThemeMode`. It applies the `.dark` class, follows the OS preference in `\"system\"` mode, and stays in sync across components and browser tabs. `DarkThemeToggle` uses it internally."},"605":{"id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode-28","page_id":"/docs/customize/dark-mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/dark-mode#dark-mode-variable-overrides","content":"A list of theme variables that are overridden when dark mode is active."},"606":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","type":"page","content":"Reboot","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Customize"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/reboot"},"607":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-0","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/reboot","content":"Reboot is a file that includes a set of CSS with element-specific changes that gives Hummingbird a clean, consistent starting point for building websites."},"608":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-1","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/reboot#css-variables","content":"CSS variables"},"609":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-2","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/reboot#headings","content":"Headings"},"610":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-3","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/reboot#paragraph","content":"Paragraph"},"611":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-4","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/reboot#links","content":"Links"},"612":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-5","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/reboot#buttons","content":"Buttons"},"613":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-6","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/reboot#horizontal-rules","content":"Horizontal rules"},"614":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-7","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/reboot#lists","content":"Lists"},"615":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-8","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/reboot#description-lists","content":"Description lists"},"616":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-9","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/reboot#code","content":"Code"},"617":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-10","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/reboot#address","content":"Address"},"618":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-11","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/reboot#blockquote","content":"Blockquote"},"619":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-12","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/reboot#legend","content":"Legend"},"620":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-13","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/reboot#captions","content":"Captions"},"621":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-14","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/customize/reboot#reboot-css-variables","content":"Reboot CSS variables"},"622":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-15","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/reboot#css-variables","content":"CSS variables provide a powerful way to customize and theme projects. It is a feature in modern CSS that allows defining reusable values directly in stylesheets. CSS variables make customization easy: change a value in one place (like `:root`) and it updates everywhere the variable is used. Variables can be set at different levels (global, component, etc.), making them flexible."},"623":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-16","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/reboot#css-variables","content":"A \"Reboot\" stylesheet (like Hummingbird's Reboot) resets browser styles and sets up a foundation for consistent design. Using CSS variables in Reboot makes it easy to customize base styles without editing the core CSS — just override the variables."},"624":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-17","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/reboot#css-variables","content":"Tailwind CSS uses CSS variables for theming and customization. Hummingbird makes use of Tailwind's CSS variable feature to define colors, typography, spacing, and more. This allows projects to easily adapt the design system to specific needs. Learn more about Hummingbird's CSS variables in the Theming section."},"625":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-18","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/reboot#css-variables","content":"Reboot is included automatically when Hummingbird CSS is imported, so JSX elements rendered by React components get these base styles with no extra setup."},"626":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-19","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/reboot#headings","content":"All the headings (`h1` to `h6`) in Hummingbird are styled with CSS variables for font size, weight, line height, and margin."},"627":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-20","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/reboot#paragraph","content":"For all paragraph (`<p>`) elements, `margin-top` was removed, and `margin-bottom: 1rem` is set."},"628":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-21","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/reboot#links","content":"Links are styled with a default `color` and an `underline`. On hover, the link color changes to a darker shade."},"629":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-22","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/reboot#buttons","content":"By default, buttons (`<button>`) have a `cursor-pointer` style. When a button is disabled, the cursor changes to `cursor-default`."},"630":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-23","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/reboot#horizontal-rules","content":"Default `margin-top` and `margin-bottom` for horizontal rules (`<hr>`) is set to `1rem`."},"631":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-24","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/reboot#lists","content":"By default, unordered lists (`<ul>`) use disc bullets, and ordered lists (`<ol>`) use decimal numbers. Both types of lists have a left padding of `2rem` and a bottom margin of `1rem`. Nested lists have no bottom margin."},"632":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-25","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/reboot#description-lists","content":"Terms (`<dt>`) are styled with a bold font weight, while descriptions (`<dd>`) use a regular font weight. Default `margin-bottom` for `<dl>` is `1rem`."},"633":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-26","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/reboot#code","content":"By default, inline code elements (`<code>`) are styled with a specific text color and font size. When a `<code>` element is nested inside an `<a>` tag, it inherits the link's text color and font size."},"634":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-27","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/reboot#address","content":"The `<address>` element is styled with a bottom margin of `1rem`."},"635":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-28","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/reboot#blockquote","content":"By default, blockquotes (`<blockquote>`) have a bottom margin of `1rem`."},"636":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-29","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/reboot#legend","content":"The `<legend>` element is styled to be a block-level element with full width, no padding, and specific margin, font weight, and font size."},"637":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-30","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/reboot#captions","content":"By default, table captions (`<caption>`) are aligned to the left and positioned at the bottom of the table. They also have specific font weight and padding."},"638":{"id":"/docs/customize/reboot-31","page_id":"/docs/customize/reboot","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/customize/reboot#reboot-css-variables","content":"The following CSS variables are defined in Hummingbird for reboot styles. Override these variables in the CSS to customize the base styles of the project."},"6